  "note": "Municipal elections, 18 May 1955. Only Clifton Ward was contested. The four uncontested wards are from the nominations printed in the News-Letter of 5 May 1955; the North Down Herald (7 May 1955) reports that after Magowan's withdrawal in Ballyholme only Clifton was contested (round 2, 7 Nov 2026). James E. Freeland 'slipped in unopposed in Dufferin where Mr. Harry Grindle did not come up for re-election' (North Down Herald, 7 May 1955, p. 1). Returned unopposed."
